$
# Note$
# Proposed: no Figma frame. The soon mock with the CVE alert:$
# two callouts, the CVE's first, a blank line between.$
$
hardn  v0.4.0              https://github.com/abbott/hardn$
$
# Alpine 3.22.4 ################################################$
$
  [BOS-SAN-L01]            192.0.2.10$
                           182 days, 2 hours, 26 minutes$
$
  [*] Risk Level           Moderate ~ medium security$
$
  [+] User                 Configured non-root, sudo$
  [+] SSH Login            Configured root disallowed$
  [+] SSH Auth             Configured key-only auth$
  [+] SSH Port             Configured non-default (2230)$
  [+] Firewall             Configured deny policy$
  [ ] Auto Updates         Not Configured$
  [ ] AppArmor             Not Configured$
$
   # Warning: CVE-2026-123158$
   # Upgrade openssh.$
   # Select option: 2) SSH Login$
$
   # Warning: Alpine 3.22 support ends 2027-05-01$
   # Upgrade to Alpine 3.24.$
$
----------------------------------------------------------------$
$
  Select an option         Mode Live$
$
   1) User Management      Create, configure (sudo, SSH keys)$
   2) SSH Login            Root login, passwords, port$
   3) Firewall             Configure ufw rules$
   4) DNS                  Configure nameservers$
   8) Run All              Execute hardening operations$
   9) Backup               Configure hardn backup$
  10) Configuration        View hardn.yml$
  11) System Details       View system information$
  12) Logs                 View log file$
$
   0) Exit                 q to quit$
$
    > Option [0-4, 8-12 or q]:$
$
$

